I come back to my flat.
I put the grocery bag on the kitchen counter.
Now I start the prep work for making Kande Pohe.
I look at my phone and listen to the video's instructions.
"First take the thick poha in a strainer and wash it," the chef says.
So, I take the poha in a big strainer.
I wash them clean under water.
Then, I keep the poha aside to soften.
After that, I take the vegetables to chop.
I take a knife and a chopping board.
First, I peel the onions.
Then, I carefully chop the onions finely.
After that, I take two green chilies.
I cut the chilies into small pieces.
Finally, I wash the fresh coriander with water.
I finely chop the coriander too.
I put all the chopped vegetables in a plate.
Now my prep work is complete.
